WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.750
From Game of Thrones to Pompeii, Kit Harington
has taken his chiseled body to screens large

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.750
and small.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.180
Reviews never fail to notice just how jacked
this dude always manages to be.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.440
We've noticed, too.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.530
Here's how he does it.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.530
Training with stunt actors

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:19.160
From Game of Thrones' brutal, body-twisting
battle scenes to the sword-and-sandal action

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:24.269
of 2014's Pompeii, Harington has had to conquer
quite a few stunts.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:27.539
Turns out, this is a solid way to get and
stay in shape.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:31.269
"Done a lot of physical training for the role.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:32.690
Training sort of six times a week."

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.880
As an actor, Harington has had to manipulate
his body in numerous ways.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.120
One of his favorite ways to push the limits
is by training with stunt actors, thus cutting

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.730
out the middleman and learning action choreography
as he trains in a way that's consistent with

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.140
the character he's playing.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:52.120
As he told Vanity Fair, his role in Pompeii
demanded daily training for four hours in

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.480
addition to a very specialized diet.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.730
Working on his swordsmanship

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.730
Harington doesn't just train like a fighter
— he wields like one, too.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:05.000
His workout routine has involved everything
from one-handed swordsmanship to dual wielding,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.490
ranging from fighting that employs lightweight
sabers to the kind that incorporates the weighty,

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.820
long-handled broadswords that Jon Snow most
commonly uses.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.750
His sword training was so intense for Pompeii
that the Game of Thrones staff noted a change

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.940
in his technique.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.230
Thanks to all that training, he returned to
the celebrated fantasy series as a much more

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.490
fluid and physically skilled actor.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:26.970
A specifically calibrated diet

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.620
Exercise is only part of getting in shape,
of course.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.070
It has to work harmoniously with a lot of
other things, from a solid sleep schedule

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.840
to adequate hydration and mental wellness.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.211
But above all, it must be paired with a well-balanced
diet, attuned to the individual's needs, and

00:01:42.211 --> 00:01:45.210
that's exactly the kind of diet Harington
follows.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.620
Here's how Harington honed himself into a
lean, mean machine for Pompeii:

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:57.330
"I went on this vigorous regime of over five
weeks of eating over 4000 calories a day."

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.260
As Harington told Men's Health, he

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.860
"was eating all the time: loads of good carbs,
like brown rice and sweet potatoes.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.670
And lots of chicken."

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.910
Of course, that can get boring fast, which
is where so many aspiring athletes fail.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.000
One of Harington's trainers said the key is
in the seasoning.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.080
With the right preparations, even the humble
sweet potato can taste a thousand different

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.080
ways.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.450
Personally, he recommends a special blend
of salt and 15 herbs called Herbamare.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.650
Cable-based workouts

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.900
Picking any one exercise can be overwhelming.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.780
While the plethora of information on everything
from hyper-specific diets to confusing weight

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.810
machines can be a boon at times, it can also
be a curse.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.840
How does one choose where to begin?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.349
How much time is any one person willing to
devote to trial and error?

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:45.780
When it comes to Harington's workouts for
Game of Thrones, there's one type of exercise

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.850
that has proven more useful than the rest:
cable-based workouts.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:55.670
His trainer, Dalton Wong, developed a program
that uses these exercises to mimic his in-character

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:56.670
moves.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.670
He told Men's Journal:

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:02.810
"We were doing… lots of cable routines that
would allow his body a fuller range of movement."

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:07.069
Given that he's usually swinging his sword
wrapped in layer upon layer of heavy fur and

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:11.900
leather, it sounds like working with flexible
cables is exactly the right course of action.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.380
Hitting the largest muscle groups

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.160
Strength training has become more and more
popular over the last few years.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.170
As Harington has spent most of his career
playing brawny dudes with physical jobs to

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.450
do, he's devout to the practice.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.709
But he doesn't just devote himself to any
old strength training regimen — he focuses

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:30.570
specifically on what will get him the best
results.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:35.319
His trainer Dalton Wong focuses specifically
on training Harington according to his largest

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:40.440
muscle groups, developing routines that strengthen
his back, legs and glutes.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.410
These exercises — largely deadlifts, lateral
lunges, and upper body push and pull movements

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:51.010
— are done for 45 minutes to an hour, at
a pace so intense the exercises double as

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.010
cardio.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:56.640
As anyone who's seen his muscled physique
on screen can attest, this routine is clearly

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:57.640
working.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:58.640
Always warming up

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:00.930
It's not enough to push one's body to the
absolute limit.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.730
The serious athlete has to spend time warming
up.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.650
Harington is dedicated to what is an essential
part of any routine, and warming up has kept

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.030
him in fighting shape.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.810
Wong shared one of the workout routines he
developed for Harington, and a good third

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.129
of it focuses solely on warm-up exercises.

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:21.090
Warming up is the kind of thing that novice
gym rats often skip, since it can seem like

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.370
such a waste of time.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:27.259
But the consequences of diving right into
training without warming up can be devastating.

00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:29.000
Instead, be like Harington.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.550
Be committed to getting your body ready for
the thorough workout that ensues.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.849
Changing up his routine

00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:39.419
When all is said and done, even the most perfectly
calibrated routine can't trump stagnation.

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:43.380
That's why having a variety of activities
is so important to staying in shape — a

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.639
tenet that Harington lives by.

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:47.509
In 2016, he noted:

00:04:47.509 --> 00:04:50.819
"The physical stuff is very much a part of
who Jon Snow is.

00:04:50.819 --> 00:04:54.659
I've got into rock climbing, ice climbing,
sword fighting, and horse riding."

00:04:54.659 --> 00:04:56.129
So what have we learned?

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:59.360
One cannot live by squats, pull-ups, or diet
alone.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.520
We have to adapt, shake it up, and try new
things.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.789
"High intensity interval training keeps me
in shape for fighting wildlings, while they

00:05:06.789 --> 00:05:08.099
increase muscle mass.

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:12.069
Helps me defend the Seven Kingdoms against
55-foot giants."

